From 9dca74550532399075ec47126b28e6d646c9851e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:04:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Far spaces: one translation for a group of accesses to one
 object

The front end records the size of the far struct object an access
lies in. Within a block, accesses through one pointer temporary inside
that object share one translation of the pointer's page (ADR-0009:
objects keep to a page). That translation stores its RAM page in one
of four pin slots, farpins, whose pages the fault handler does not
evict. A call or a new value of the pointer ends a group, and groups
that overlap take different slots.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
